$
  T : T' :: D^m : D'^m :: phi^(m/2) : phi'^(m/2),
$
in which we represent by $T$ and $T'$ the time of a certain number of oscillations for metallic wires of which the diameters are $D$ and $D'$ and the weights for the same length are $phi$ and $phi'$; $m$ is the power that we are trying to determine. From this proportion we obtain
$
  m = (2 (log dot T - log dot T')) / (log dot phi - log dot phi'),
$
and this formula is to be compared with experiment.

